              </li>
            </ul>
            <p class="mt-3 text-xs text-slate-500">
              *Typical timelines; individual results vary.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ============ 2. ANSWER-FIRST TL;DR ============ -->
      <section id="answer" class="mx-auto -mt-10 max-w-5xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
        <div
          class="rounded-2xl border border-indigo-100 bg-white p-6 shadow-xl shadow-indigo-100/50 ring-1 ring-indigo-500/5 sm:p-8"
        >
          <div class="flex flex-col gap-4 sm:flex-row sm:items-start">
            <span
              class="flex h-11 w-11 flex-none items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-indigo-600 text-white shadow-md shadow-indigo-600/20"
            >
              <svg
                xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
                viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                fill="none"
                stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="2"
                stroke-linecap="round"
                stroke-linejoin="round"
                class="h-5 w-5"
                aria-hidden="true"
              >
                <path d="M13 2 4 14h7l-1 8 9-12h-7l1-8Z"></path>
              </svg>
            </span>
            <div>
              <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
                <span
                  class="inline-block rounded-full bg-indigo-50 px-2 py-0.5 text-[10px] font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-indigo-700"
                  >Quick Answer</span
                >
                <span
                  class="text-[10px] font-medium uppercase tracking-widest text-slate-400"
                  >~50 words</span
                >
              </div>
              <h2
                id="answer-title"
                class="mt-2 text-xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900 sm:text-2xl"
              >
                Back Pain Relief &amp; Posture Correction in Brief
              </h2>
              <p class="mt-3 text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-700">
                Back pain relief and posture correction start with a daily
                5-minute routine: open the chest with thoracic extension,
                activate the core, adjust your workstation, and repeat
                consistently. Most people feel less muscle tension within 7–10
                days; visible posture alignment often takes 4–6 weeks. Use the
                routine below and seek clinical care for severe or persistent
                pain.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ============ 3. THREE-COLUMN PILLAR GRID ============ -->
      <section
        id="routine"
        class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-20 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 lg:py-24"
      >
        <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl text-center">
          <span
            class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-indigo-600"
            >The Three Pillars</span
          >
          <h2
            class="mt-3 text-balance text-3xl font-black tracking-tight text-slate-900 sm:text-4xl"
          >
            The 3 Pillars of Back Pain Relief &amp; Posture Correction
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-4 text-slate-600">
            Each pillar targets a different mechanism. Do all three for a
            complete, evidence-informed routine.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-12 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-3">
          <!-- Card 1 -->
          <article
            class="group relative flex flex-col rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6 shadow-sm transition hover:-translate-y-0.5 hover:border-indigo-300 hover:shadow-lg"
          >
            <span
              class="flex h-12 w-12 items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-indigo-50 text-indigo-600 transition group-hover:bg-indigo-600 group-hover:text-white"
            >
              <svg
                xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
                viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                fill="none"
                stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="2"
                stroke-linecap="round"
                stroke-linejoin="round"
                class="h-6 w-6"
                aria-hidden="true"
              >
                <path d="M3 12h4l2-6 4 12 2-6h6"></path>
              </svg>
            </span>
            <h3 class="mt-5 text-lg font-bold text-slate-900">
              1. Thoracic Extension &amp; Chest Opening
            </h3>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600">
              Counter rounded shoulders with gentle thoracic extension, doorway
              chest stretches, and controlled breathing. Keep range comfortable
              and avoid forcing the neck.
            </p>
            <ul class="mt-4 space-y-1.5 text-sm text-slate-600">
              <li class="flex gap-2">
                <svg
                  xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
                  viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                  fill="none"
                  stroke="currentColor"
                  stroke-width="2.5"
                  stroke-linecap="round"
                  stroke-linejoin="round"
                  class="mt-0.5 h-4 w-4 flex-none text-emerald-600"
                  aria-hidden="true"
                >
                  <path d="m5 12 5 5L20 7"></path>
                </svg>
                Doorway chest opener — 30s × 2
              </li>
              <li class="flex gap-2">
                <svg
                  xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
                  viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                  fill="none"
                  stroke="currentColor"
                  stroke-width="2.5"
                  stroke-linecap="round"
                  stroke-linejoin="round"
                  class="mt-0.5 h-4 w-4 flex-none text-emerald-600"
                  aria-hidden="true"
                >
                  <path d="m5 12 5 5L20 7"></path>
                </svg>
                Foam roller thoracic extension — 60s
              </li>
              <li class="flex gap-2">
                <svg
                  xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
                  viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                  fill="none"
                  stroke="currentColor"
                  stroke-width="2.5"
                  stroke-linecap="round"
                  stroke-linejoin="round"
                  class="mt-0.5 h-4 w-4 flex-none text-emerald-600"
                  aria-hidden="true"
                >
                  <path d="m5 12 5 5L20 7"></path>
                </svg>
                Wall angels — 8–10 reps
              </li>
            </ul>
          </article>

          <!-- Card 2 -->
          <article
            class="group relative flex flex-col rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6 shadow-sm transition hover:-translate-y-0.5 hover:border-indigo-300 hover:shadow-lg"
          >
            <span
              class="flex h-12 w-12 items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-indigo-50 text-indigo-600 transition group-hover:bg-indigo-600 group-hover:text-white"
            >
              <svg
                xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
                viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                fill="none"
                stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="2"
                stroke-linecap="round"
                stroke-linejoin="round"
                class="h-6 w-6"
                aria-hidden="true"
              >
                <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle>
                <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="5"></circle>
                <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="1.5" fill="currentColor"></circle>
              </svg>
            </span>
            <h3 class="mt-5 text-lg font-bold text-slate-900">
              2. Core Activation &amp; Spinal Stability
            </h3>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600">
              Use dead bugs, bird dogs, and low-impact bracing to build trunk
              control. The goal is steady, pain-free activation — not maximal
              exertion.
            </p>
            <ul class="mt-4 space-y-1.5 text-sm text-slate-600">
              <li class="flex gap-2">
                <svg
                  xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
                  viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                  fill="none"
                  stroke="currentColor"
                  stroke-width="2.5"
                  stroke-linecap="round"
                  stroke-linejoin="round"
                  class="mt-0.5 h-4 w-4 flex-none text-emerald-600"
                  aria-hidden="true"
                >
                  <path d="m5 12 5 5L20 7"></path>
                </svg>
                Dead bugs — 6–8 per side
              </li>
              <li class="flex gap-2">
                <svg
                  xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
                  viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                  fill="none"
                  stroke="currentColor"
                  stroke-width="2.5"
                  stroke-linecap="round"
                  stroke-linejoin="round"
                  class="mt-0.5 h-4 w-4 flex-none text-emerald-600"
                  aria-hidden="true"
                >
                  <path d="m5 12 5 5L20 7"></path>
                </svg>
                Bird dogs — 6–8 per side
              </li>
              <li class="flex gap-2">
                <svg
                  xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
                  viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                  fill="none"
                  stroke="currentColor"
                  stroke-width="2.5"
                  stroke-linecap="round"
                  stroke-linejoin="round"
                  class="mt-0.5 h-4 w-4 flex-none text-emerald-600"
                  aria-hidden="true"
                >
                  <path d="m5 12 5 5L20 7"></path>
                </svg>
                Low-impact bracing — 3 × 10s holds
              </li>
            </ul>
          </article>

          <!-- Card 3 -->
          <article
            class="group relative flex flex-col rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6 shadow-sm transition hover:-translate-y-0.5 hover:border-indigo-300 hover:shadow-lg"
          >
            <span
              class="flex h-12 w-12 items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-indigo-50 text-indigo-600 transition group-hover:bg-indigo-600 group-hover:text-white"
            >
              <svg
                xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
                viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                fill="none"
                stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="2"
                stroke-linecap="round"
                stroke-linejoin="round"
                class="h-6 w-6"
                aria-hidden="true"
              >
                <rect x="3" y="4" width="18" height="12" rx="2"></rect>
                <path d="M8 20h8M12 16v4"></path>
              </svg>
            </span>
            <h3 class="mt-5 text-lg font-bold text-slate-900">
              3. Ergonomic Workstation Setup
            </h3>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600">
              Set screen height, elbow angle, feet support, and movement breaks.
              A neutral setup reduces sustained load and supports the daily
              routine.
            </p>
            <ul class="mt-4 space-y-1.5 text-sm text-slate-600">
              <li class="flex gap-2">
                <svg
                  xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
                  viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                  fill="none"
                  stroke="currentColor"
                  stroke-width="2.5"
                  stroke-linecap="round"
                  stroke-linejoin="round"
                  class="mt-0.5 h-4 w-4 flex-none text-emerald-600"
                  aria-hidden="true"
                >
                  <path d="m5 12 5 5L20 7"></path>
                </svg>
                Screen top at eye level
              </li>
              <li class="flex gap-2">
                <svg
                  xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
                  viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                  fill="none"
                  stroke="currentColor"
                  stroke-width="2.5"
                  stroke-linecap="round"
                  stroke-linejoin="round"
                  class="mt-0.5 h-4 w-4 flex-none text-emerald-600"
                  aria-hidden="true"
                >
                  <path d="m5 12 5 5L20 7"></path>
                </svg>
                Elbows at ~90° with relaxed shoulders
              </li>
              <li class="flex gap-2">
                <svg
                  xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
                  viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                  fill="none"
                  stroke="currentColor"
                  stroke-width="2.5"
                  stroke-linecap="round"
                  stroke-linejoin="round"
                  class="mt-0.5 h-4 w-4 flex-none text-emerald-600"
                  aria-hidden="true"
                >
                  <path d="m5 12 5 5L20 7"></path>
                </svg>
                Movement break every 30–45 min
              </li>
            </ul>
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ============ 4. SIDE-BY-SIDE COMPARISON TABLE ============ -->
      <section id="comparison" class="bg-slate-900 text-slate-100">
        <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-20 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 lg:py-24">
          <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl text-center">
            <span
              class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-sky-400"
              >Compare Approaches</span
            >
